// Title: Potential Signing Bypass Via Windows Developer Features
// Rule ID: a383dec4-deec-4e6e-913b-ed9249670848
// Severity: high
// Tags: attack.defense-evasion
// Category: process_creation
// Product: windows
// Pipeline: microsoft_xdr
// Source: /home/user/Sigma_KQL/sigma_rules/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_systemsettingsadminflows_turn_on_dev_features.yml
//
// Generated by sigma-to-kql converter
// Sigma rules: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma
// pySigma Kusto backend: https://github.com/AttackIQ/pySigma-backend-kusto

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\SystemSettingsAdminFlows.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "SystemSettingsAdminFlows.EXE") and ProcessCommandLine contains "TurnOnDeveloperFeatures" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "DeveloperUnlock" or ProcessCommandLine contains "EnableSideloading")